I fixed #966 (--print writing the answer twice), commented on it and closed it. I didn't comment on the other seven issues because this session did no work on them.

#966:
• **The fix:** with `--print` or `--output-format json`, the streamed text no longer goes to stdout; only the final answer is written there, once. Against the local test server, --print output went from the answer twice (with extra blank lines) to {"answer": 42} once. The json mode had the same bug, which made | jq fail with "Extra data"; it now outputs a single JSON value. Plain -p without --print still streams as before.
• **The test:** `tests/print_stdout_contract.rs` runs the real binary against a local fake API server. I re-ran it just now and all 4 tests pass. Run against the code from before the fix, the three output tests failed and the plain -p check still passed, so they do catch the original bug.
• **Still open:** when a run actually uses tools, their progress lines still print to stdout, so `--print` output isn't fully clean yet in that case. The docs say so, and I mentioned it in the comment. It's not filed as its own issue yet.

